hose existence and shape do not depend on the assessment outcome. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | GA-readiness assessment producing the definitive GA scope. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 | Versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases, plus assessment-driven hardening (error handling, scale limits). |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | E003 | Documented SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix. |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | E004 | TrustyAI-owned epic; the integration spans TrustyAI and Llama Stack distributions — assigned to TrustyAI as the most-relevant canonical component (see Component Mapping). |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | E005 | Default enablement for entitled clusters, removing the TP opt-in gate. |\n| HLR-6 | P2 | E006 | docs-authoring epic; priority P0 derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` per the docs-authoring priority exception (Step 4), not from HLR-6's P2 label. It does not push priority upstream — E004 and E005 remain P1. |\n\nAll six HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements, no bundled lower-priority HLRs.\n\n## Component Mapping\n\n- All strategy components (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard) exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (rhoai-3.0) — no new-component onboarding chains are needed; all are Konflux-onboarded per their context files, so no konflux-onboarding or license-validation epics apply.\n- Canonical component names used verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`: `Llama Stack`, `TrustyAI`, `Dashboard`, `Documentation`.\n- HLR-4's integration work spans TrustyAI (guardrails services) and Llama Stack (safety surface in the distribution). Assigned the single canonical component `TrustyAI` per the one-component-per-epic constraint; the TrustyAI team owns the supported-integration deliverable. If Llama Stack-distribution-side wiring changes turn out to be required, they are coordinated with RHOAI GenAI within that