{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0922ccee-6003-4d5e-8d88-7344207594f3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a36341b6cc4a6c9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-bqjlabos/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and GA hardening\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama Stack: versioned APIs, a published deprecation policy, a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases, and remediation of the quality gaps (error handling, scale limits) identified by the GA-readiness assessment. It converts the Tech Preview component into one whose published API surface carries a stability commitment.\n\n## Description of dependency\n\nThis epic's scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: until the assessment lands, the size of the stability and hardening work is an estimate. The assessment's gap inventory rewrites this epic's remediation scope; the versioned-API, deprecation-policy, and upgrade-path deliverables are fixed by the strategy and proceed once the assessment defines the hardening scope around them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Introduce API versioning for the published API surface of the Llama Stack distribution.\n- Define and publish a deprecation policy for the published API surface.\n- Implement and test an upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases, including migration of existing LlamaStackDistribution custom resources.\n- Remediate GA-blocking gaps in error handling across the API surface and operator, as identified by the GA-readiness assessment.\n- Remediate GA-blocking scale-limit gaps as identified by the GA-readiness assessment, including documenting validated limits.\n- Address every gap the GA-readiness assessment marks GA-blocking within this component's surfaces.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is applied consistently across the surface.\n- A deprecation policy is published covering the versioned API surface.\n- An upgrade from each of the last two Tech Preview releases to the GA candidate is tested and passes, including custom-resource migration, with the procedure documented as part of the upgrade deliverable.\n- Every gap the GA-readiness assessment marked GA-blocking and assigned to this component's surfaces has a merged remediation or an explicit, reviewed waiver recorded with a reason.\n- Error-handling behavior on the published API surface returns structured, documented errors for failure cases identified in the assessment.\n- Scale limits validated during remediation are recorded and handed to the support-posture work for inclusion in the supported configuration matrix.\n- Rollback/compatibility: consumers of the existing TP API surface are not broken without a deprecation-policy-compliant path (the strategy replaces TP behavior with GA guarantees).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. This epic delivers HLR-2 in full, plus the assessment-driven hardening scope produced under HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32155,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa30f851d0b911ff","agent_id":"a3c9d019b51fdd077","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"a584dc46-9403-46b1-8cc5-f69db2f1a87b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:14:41.250Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
