sent, the Dashboard shows Llama Stack management surfaces with no opt-in action required by the user.\n46\t- On a cluster without the required entitlement, the Llama Stack management surfaces remain hidden.\n47\t- The Tech Preview opt-in gate for Llama Stack management no longer appears in the Dashboard.\n48\t- The default-on state passes the Dashboard's existing feature-integration test coverage for the Llama Stack management surfaces.\n49\t- Feature-flag defaults and configuration documentation reflect the default-on behavior.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- **HLR-5 (P1)**: The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic delivers HLR-5 in full.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-976000905faba207","agent_id":"a8e4cf2fbe6a4144c","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"f98a8367-11bd-4c62-bc20-a3ffcaac7f7f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:17:34.690Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-964099eb3a89db9c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
