{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7ba2ba7eed9ae5d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tscore: 10\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: 'Missing DAG edge E002 -> E003: E002''s AC records validated scale\n10\t    limits \"handed to the support-posture work for inclusion in the supported configuration\n11\t    matrix\" and E003''s scope/ACs incorporate those handed-over limits, but neither\n12\t    the frontmatter dependencies nor the summary diagram has the edge. The summary''s\n13\t    justification (\"No shared artifact: parallel\") is contradicted by both epics''\n14\t    content. Add E002 to E003''s dependencies (and a matching diagram edge); this\n15\t    also orders E003 after E001 transitively, covering the GA-scope alignment in E003''s\n16\t    scope.'\n17\t- severity: minor\n18\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n19\t  description: 'E004 human_process_gates: 0 is arguable: conferring supported status\n20\t    on the integration and reaching the cross-team support/triage agreement (an E004\n21\t    AC) imply product/support acceptance analogous to E003''s -1; re-score or strengthen\n22\t    the rationale.'\n23\t- severity: minor\n24\t  criterion: Acceptance Criteria Quality\n25\t  description: E004 AC \"validation pass covering the guardrails capabilities the strategy\n26\t    commits to at GA\" is slightly vague — the strategy enumerates no specific guardrails\n27\t    capabilities, so the validation scope is circular; name the capability list or\n28\t    concrete validation surface (functional coverage, failure behavior, configuration\n29\t    paths).\n30\terror: null\n31\t---\n32\t## Review Summary\n33\t\n34\tScore: 10/14 — fail\n35\tRecommendation: revise\n36\t\n37\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-9014` exited 0 — epic body\n38\tsections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n39\timplementation-type parallelism, and shared-surface enforcement all pass). Triage check:\n40\t`triage: null` (full decomposition), so the 6-epic output is expected shape. The failure\n41\tbelow is a DAG-completeness defect the validator cannot see: an artifact handover\n42\tdescribed in two epics' own text is missing from the DAG.\n43\t\n44\t## Criterion Details\n45\t\n46\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n47\tAll six HLRs map to exactly one epic each, and the traceability matrix is present in the\n48\tsummary with per-epic HLR Traceability sections matching. Priority inheritance holds:\n49\tE002 (P0) is gated only by E001 (P0). E006 is P0 via the documented docs-authoring\n50\texception (strategy `priority: Critical`), and per that exception it does not push P0\n51\tonto E004/E005. No priority collapse: every HLR has its own epic; E002's inclusion of\n52\tassessment-driven hardening is HLR-1's output feeding HLR-2's work, not a bundled\n53\tdeferrable lower-priority HLR.\n54\t\n55\t### 2. DAG Coherence (0/2)\n56\tDiagram/frontmatter consistency is good: every diagram edge (dependency → dependent)\n57\tmatches the target epic's `dependencies` (E002: [E001]; E006: [E002, E003, E004, E005];\n58\tall others empty), no circular or invalid edges, no konflux-onboarding or\n59\tlicense-validation epics so Rules 7/8/10 pairings don't apply, and critical path length\n60\t3 (E001 → E002 → E006) is reasonable for this strategy size. However, there is a\n61\t**critical missing edge: E002 → E003**. E002's acceptance criteria state \"Scale limits\n62\tvalidated during remediation are recorded and handed to the support-posture work for\n63\tinclusion in the supported configuration matrix,\" and E003's scope and ACs consume that\n64\thandover (\"incorporates the validated scale limits handed over from the stability and\n65\thardening work\"). This is an explicit data/artifact dependency discoverable from epic\n66\tcontent, and the DAG-justification table's claim for the absent edge — \"No shared\n67\tartifact: parallel\" — is directly contradicted by both epics' own text. Without the\n68\tedge, E003 can complete before the limits it is required to incorporate exist, making\n69\tits AC unsatisfiable without rework. This is not a build-pipeline output consumed as\n70\tcontent (the AC-gate exception covers image digests/attestations/SBOMs, not a\n71\tdeliverable handed between epics); Rule 15's parallel-by-default for same component +\n72\tteam applies only when no shared artifact exists, which is not the case here. Note\n73\talso that E003's scope aligns the matrix with \"the GA scope defined by the readiness\n74\tassessment\" (E001 output) with no E001 → E003 edge; the summary's AC-not-edge\n75\trationale is arguable on its own, and adding E002 → E003 orders E003 after E001\n76\ttransitively, resolving it. A critical issue forces 0 for this criterion.\n77\t\n78\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n79\tEach epic has a distinct component/team tuple drawn from the canonical list (Llama\n80\tStack, TrustyAI, Dashboard, Documentation — verified against\n81\t`.context/rhai-components.txt`). E004's integration spans TrustyAI and Llama Stack\n82\tdistribution surfaces but is one logical change (HLR-4 treats it as one capability)\n83\tassigned to the single canonical component TrustyAI with documented rationale — an\n84\tacceptable boundary call, not a violation. E002 is estimated at 4–6 weeks (above the\n85\t~2-week guideline) but is correctly classified as one logical change over one API\n86\tsurface set, and the Health Warnings carry all three required elements: estimate,\n87\trationale, and a concrete conditional re-split trigger (re-split by gap category once\n88\tthe assessment lands) — watch item only, no dock. No scope duplication: E006's\n89\tguardrails-integration documentation topic consumes E004's delivered integration docs\n90\t(Rule 11 consolidation), it does not independently re