{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d235fabad1f2406","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: no systematic GA-readiness assessment of Llama Stack has been done, TP feedback is scattered across support tickets, and the full inventory of gaps between current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar is not yet known. The epic produces the definitive GA scope — a gap inventory and remediation plan across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling — that determines the size and content of the downstream stability and hardening work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Collect and consolidate Tech Preview feedback from support tickets and other feedback channels into a single triaged list.\n34\t- Assess the current published API surface against GA stability requirements (versioning state, deprecation posture, breaking changes across recent TP releases).\n35\t- Assess the upgrade story: what upgrade paths exist today between the last two TP releases, and what testing has been done.\n36\t- Assess scale limits: documented or observed limits of the current distribution under GA-representative workloads.\n37\t- Assess error handling quality across the API surface and operator.\n38\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document: a prioritized gap inventory with remediation estimates, explicitly identifying which gaps are GA-blocking and which are not.\n39\t- Flag any gap whose remediation would change the approach or structure of the stability and hardening work.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A single GA-readiness assessment document exists that inventories gaps in all four enumerated areas: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n44\t- Every gap entry states the current TP behavior, the GA bar it fails to meet, and a remediation estimate.\n45\t- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated and each item is either mapped to a gap entry or explicitly ruled out of GA scope with a reason.\n46\t- The document identifies which gaps are GA-blocking, producing a definitive GA scope that the stability and hardening work can be planned against.\n47\t- Gaps whose remediation would require a different approach than API versioning and hardening (e.g., architectural rework) are explicitly called out.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is the direct delivery of HLR-1.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaec3bbc2be06058","agent_id":"a602e19a0ce932531","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"b6d144a7-e687-4e15-b003-17076712f6dc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:50.772Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d235fabad1f2406","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
