{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e12bf2328477f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and GA hardening\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the GA scope materially\n15\t    larger or smaller than estimated, this epic's hardening scope is rewritten to\n16\t    the assessment's remediation inventory; if it finds no GA-blocking gaps, hardening\n17\t    reduces to the versioned-API, deprecation-policy, and upgrade-path deliverables.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and GA hardening\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama Stack: versioned APIs, a published deprecation policy, a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases, and remediation of the quality gaps (error handling, scale limits) identified by the GA-readiness assessment. It converts the Tech Preview component into one whose published API surface carries a stability commitment.\n40\t\n41\t## Gating Dependency\n42\t\n43\tThis epic's scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: until the assessment lands, the size of the stability and hardening work is an estimate. The assessment's gap inventory rewrites this epic's remediation scope; the versioned-API, deprecation-policy, and upgrade-path deliverables are fixed by the strategy and proceed once the assessment defines the hardening scope around them.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Introduce API versioning for the published API surface of the Llama Stack distribution.\n48\t- Define and publish a deprecation policy for the published API surface.\n49\t- Implement and test an upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases, including migration of existing LlamaStackDistribution custom resources.\n50\t- Remediate GA-blocking gaps in error handling across the API surface and operator, as identified by the GA-readiness assessment.\n51\t- Remediate GA-blocking scale-limit gaps as identified by the GA-readiness assessment, including documenting validated limits.\n52\t- Address every gap the GA-readiness assessment marks GA-blocking within this component's surfaces.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is applied consistently across the surface.\n57\t- A deprecation policy is published covering the versioned API surface.\n58\t- An upgrade from each of the last two Tech Preview releases to the GA candidate is tested and passes, including custom-resource migration, with the procedure documented as part of the upgrade deliverable.\n59\t- Every gap the GA-readiness assessment marked GA-blocking and assigned to this component's surfaces has a merged remediation or an explicit, reviewed waiver recorded with a reason.\n60\t- Error-handling behavior on the published API surface returns structured, documented errors for failure cases identified in the assessment.\n61\t- Scale limits validated during remediation are recorded and handed to the support-posture work for inclusion in the supported configuration matrix.\n62\t- Rollback/compatibility: consumers of the existing TP API surface are not broken without a deprecation-policy-compliant path (the strategy replaces TP behavior with GA guarantees).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. This epic delivers HLR-2 in full, plus the assessment-driven hardening scope produced under HLR-1.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaec3bbc2be06058","agent_id":"a602e19a0ce932531","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"059e53ca-c24e-4591-9e90-982ba7ed987d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:51.740Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e12bf2328477f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
