42\t- Publish these artifacts through the support and product channels used for GA platform components.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- SLO targets are documented and published for the GA distribution.\n47\t- A backport policy is documented and published, covering release lines, fix eligibility, and security-fix handling.\n48\t- A supported configuration matrix is documented and published, enumerating supported provider, version, and deployment combinations.\n49\t- The configuration matrix incorporates the validated scale limits handed over from the stability and hardening work where applicable.\n50\t- The support-posture artifacts are reviewed and accepted by the owning product and support organizations.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic delivers HLR-3 in full.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaec3bbc2be06058","agent_id":"a602e19a0ce932531","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"a0c43a60-d54e-4f0b-87d3-549f5628d263","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:54.181Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89fe1592eea8b91c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
