{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b984fee19bb46ad5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the safety-guardrails integration via TrustyAI a supported, documented integration for GA Llama Stack distributions, promoted from an experimental flag. The TrustyAI team owns the integration deliverable; where changes on the Llama Stack distribution side are needed to complete the integration, they are coordinated with the Llama Stack owning team within this epic's scope.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration for Llama Stack distributions from experimental-flag status to supported status.\n38\t- Validate the integration against GA-bar quality criteria: functional coverage of the guardrails surface, failure behavior, and configuration paths that supported customers will use.\n39\t- Document the integration: supported configuration, capabilities, and limitations, suitable for inclusion in GA product documentation.\n40\t- Define and record the support posture for the integration (how issues are triaged between the TrustyAI and Llama Stack support surfaces).\n41\t- Remove or graduate the experimental flag so the integration is available as a supported path in GA distributions.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The guardrails integration is enabled through a supported (non-experimental) configuration path in GA Llama Stack distributions.\n46\t- The integration passes a validation pass over three concrete surfaces — functional coverage of the guardrails capabilities exposed through the integration, failure behavior (how guardrails requests degrade and report when TrustyAI services are unavailable or misconfigured), and the supported configuration paths — with failures either fixed or documented as explicit limitations.\n47\t- Documentation of the integration (setup, capabilities, limitations) is complete and technically reviewed against the implemented behavior.\n48\t- The support/triage path for integration issues is defined and agreed between the TrustyAI and Llama Stack teams.\n49\t- No experimental or TP label remains on the integration in GA distribution artifacts or documentation.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic delivers HLR-4 in full.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaec3bbc2be06058","agent_id":"a602e19a0ce932531","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"afe79676-740f-4efc-9638-1031521eb76b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:54.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b984fee19bb46ad5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
