ation for GA distributions (setup, capabilities, limitations).\n46\t  - Dashboard default-enablement behavior for entitled clusters.\n47\t  - Removal or update of all Tech Preview caveats, experimental labels, and opt-in instructions across Llama Stack documentation topics.\n48\t- Author all topics to Red Hat GA documentation standards and migrate them through the Red Hat docs content process.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Documentation covers every topic in the content outline above, at GA standard.\n53\t- A migration guide exists that walks a TP user through upgrading to GA, consistent with the tested upgrade path delivered by the stability work.\n54\t- No Llama Stack documentation topic retains Tech Preview or experimental labeling for GA-supported behavior.\n55\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented GA behavior (the delivered API stability, support posture, guardrails integration, and Dashboard enablement), and review findings are resolved.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- **HLR-6 (P2)**: Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including migration notes from TP. This epic delivers HLR-6 in full.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaec3bbc2be06058","agent_id":"a602e19a0ce932531","session_id":"ee65eb59-0a07-4c88-ab7a-b3f887908170","uuid":"e81db2df-ee11-442f-93cb-04abe4ed967a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:23:58.563Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-922c1f6d140b225b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
